Falsifies `device_tree_blob::verification::decode_regions_stays_inside_its_output`.

The defect: `decode_regions` indexes `out[n]` in place of `out.get_mut(n)` and its
`TooManyRegions` refusal. Both spellings read as "store the next region"; the indexed one panics
when a `reg` property holds more nonempty pairs than the caller gave slots, and a panic in the boot
parser is a boot that stops on input the firmware chose.

Expected to fail: the bounds check on `out[n]`, for any value of three nonempty, non-wrapping pairs
under one-cell addresses and sizes (24 bytes, two slots).

diff --git a/src/lib.rs b/src/lib.rs
--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -1181,7 +1181,7 @@
             return Err(Error::RegionOverflow);
         }
 
-        *out.get_mut(n).ok_or(Error::TooManyRegions)? = Region {
+        out[n] = Region {
             start,
             size_bytes: size,
         };
